Rules:
  [G1] Use gRPC for internal service communication.
  [G2] Use REST/GraphQL only for external APIs.
  [G3] Implement circuit breakers for external calls.
  [G4] Use structured logging with request IDs.
  [G5] Implement health checks (liveness and readiness).
  [G6] Use message brokers (Kafka/NATS) for async communication.
  [G7] Implement distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry.
  [G8] Use service mesh (Istio/Linkerd) for production.
  [G9] Implement graceful shutdown with signal handling.
  [G10] Use config management (Vault/env) for secrets.

Pros:
  - Scalable architecture
  - Independent deployment
  - Technology flexibility

Cons:
  - Operational complexity
  - Network latency
  - Debugging distributed systems

Alternatives:
  - Monolith
  - Modular monolith
  - Serverless

State: +

